                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b48b6847-84cc-3d25-90fd-1ee34f92ec54",
                        "entry_id": "c0197808-887b-3e50-a94b-17b217a9656e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "gepanzerter Fußsoldat im antiken Griechenland"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b92ca35f-3746-4036-9f7a-7f6b340385e9",
                                "sense_id": "b48b6847-84cc-3d25-90fd-1ee34f92ec54",
                                "text": "Während des Peloponnesischen Krieges waren Hopliten wichtiger Bestandteil der Heere."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5967dd73-3ba5-4850-984b-16e16ced2c19",
                                "sense_id": "b48b6847-84cc-3d25-90fd-1ee34f92ec54",
                                "text": "Die Hopliten kämpften in einer Phalanx."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d3fb7375-df74-4547-8a25-72460ac942c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0197808-887b-3e50-a94b-17b217a9656e",
                        "source_sense_id": "b48b6847-84cc-3d25-90fd-1ee34f92ec54",
                        "source_sense_description": "historisch: gepanzerter Fußsoldat im antiken Griechenland",
                        "target_lang_word": "hoplite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hoplite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f923a8a1-fb04-36c5-877a-38b7a638687c",
                                        "entry_id": "eab6b4c6-6382-3164-b420-318934f75b47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A heavily-armed infantry soldier of Ancient Greece, wielding a one-handed spear and an aspis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb84fcb9-b462-4e7d-a97b-04ceae39af24",
                                                "sense_id": "f923a8a1-fb04-36c5-877a-38b7a638687c",
                                                "text": "[…] it was in the line of \"hoplites\" that the mass of citizen-soldiers were to be found."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e76b50d7-ede5-4349-963a-aa3b0175e606",
                                                "sense_id": "f923a8a1-fb04-36c5-877a-38b7a638687c",
                                                "text": "However important the use of hoplites against, or in support of, troops of other arms had become, their chief function was still to fight other hoplites, though the battles of the early fourth century were very different from the ponderous confrontations that had filled King Xerxes and his courtiers with contempt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cb30e20-9ad9-4772-a1fe-740d3714a914",
                                                "sense_id": "f923a8a1-fb04-36c5-877a-38b7a638687c",
                                                "text": "The Athenian hoplites who routed the Persian invaders on the field of Marathon in 490 created one of the great 'myths' of Athens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a75bd02-00e8-4701-9a21-f607c06af771",
                                                "sense_id": "f923a8a1-fb04-36c5-877a-38b7a638687c",
                                                "text": "Yet this war of ideals was also a war of many truces, for there were many grounds for accommodation between generals and hoplites. Generals were drawn from the ranks of the hoplites, as hoplites they fought; when they ceased to be generals, it was to the hoplite ranks that they returned. Such was the power of hoplite ideals that many commanders were delighted to compete as hoplites rather than as tacticians, as their frequent deaths in the line signify."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "74714100-3206-4926-933f-1e2418a745dd",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0197808-887b-3e50-a94b-17b217a9656e",
                        "source_sense_id": "b48b6847-84cc-3d25-90fd-1ee34f92ec54",
                        "source_sense_description": "historisch: gepanzerter Fußsoldat im antiken Griechenland",
                        "target_lang_word": "hoplite",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hoplite",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e95b966-eb32-31aa-960f-77078e9bfa9b",
                                        "entry_id": "bd2e8b1a-9c4c-3650-a109-6160748c155c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fantassin grec pesamment armé, qui avait pour armes défensives le casque, le bouclier, la cuirasse, les bottines, garnies de fer ; pour armes offensives la pique et l’épée."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient-Greek"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dde72c90-debe-44f3-b0a9-e1ffbf3e5aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "9e95b966-eb32-31aa-960f-77078e9bfa9b",
                                                "text": "Ce que nous voyons de plus clair, c’est que la force de l’armée était dans la grosse infanterie, l’infanterie des Hoplites, comme disaient les grecs, et qui, dans la tactique de cette époque tenait le premier rang."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db3d7a66-2fc4-4d30-86b1-6f2673b9a342",
                                                "sense_id": "9e95b966-eb32-31aa-960f-77078e9bfa9b",
                                                "text": "À l’intérieur de la cité, elles confirment l’ascension politique des thètes, la classe de citoyens la moins fortunée : incapables de payer l’équipement militaire d’un hoplite, les thètes servent comme rameurs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
